     "text": "Assuming **one adult, one-way, from Orlando International (MCO) to Atlanta (ATL)** on **November 14, 2026**:\n\n| Airline | Flight | Advertised price | Where to book |\n|---|---|---:|---|\n| Frontier | Nonstop, 4:48 p.m.–6:37 p.m. | **$55 USD one-way** | Trip.com’s Orlando–Atlanta flight listing. ([us.trip.com](https://us.trip.com/flights/airport-mco-atl?utm_source=openai)) |\n\n**Important:** I found this advertised fare, but couldn’t verify that it is **regular economy rather than basic economy**, or confirm the final checkout total. It’s a booking lead—not a confirmed price matching all your requirements.\n\nFrontier’s own website also advertises **from $44 for November 14**, but its disclaimer says membership may be required and includes conflicting round-trip wording, so I wouldn’t treat $44 as a confirmed one-way price. ([flights.flyfrontier.com](https://flights.flyfrontier.com/en/flights-from-orlando-to-atlanta))\n\nWhen booking, select November 14, one-way, one adult, and decline optional bags, paid seat selection, insurance, and bundles.\n\nSOURCES: Trip.com; Frontier Airlines (flights.flyfrontier.com).",
